  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "Conserved hydration sites and interactome-wide interface modelling now connect missense pathogenicity to protein structure at scale.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the use of protein structure to contextualize variant effects. A bioRxiv preprint applies AI-based structural modelling to 109,282 human protein interaction structures, characterizing interfaces and mapping pathogenic variants onto predicted interfaces. A second preprint, memVar, integrates roughly 10.9M ClinVar, COSMIC and gnomAD SNVs across 7,732 membrane proteins with topology, lipid contacts and interaction data. The published study reports that conserved water molecule sites in PDB structures are enriched for pathogenic missense variants, and uses MD simulations of GCase to link disruption of these sites to pathogenicity. What is new is the identification of conserved hydration sites as a structural correlate of missense pathogenicity. The microbiome PheWAS is unrelated to structure and sits outside this thread, so the shared element is structural contextualization rather than a common mechanism.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
